A composite literal initializing a state var reads its neighbors, and every
element of it has to be lowered with the same context the var's own scope has.

A struct, list or map literal looks like a constant, and both the Go and the
Kotlin backends took that shape as a license to lower it without a context --
`golang.IRLiteralToGo` and `kotlin.IRLiteralToKt`, whose whole vocabulary is
literals nested in literals. A field initialized from a model var is an
`ir.Ident`, which neither walk has a case for, and the case-less answer is the
empty string. So `P{a = a, b = b}` came out `P{A: "", B: ""}` on go and
`P(a = "", b = "")` on kotlin: the field's value and its *type* both wrong, the
build exiting 0. `[]int{"", ""}` does not even compile.

`constPair` is the same literal with constants in it, and it is here because it
is the case that always worked -- substituting `const` for `var` was what
isolated the fault to the read rather than to the literal. Both spellings are
now lowered by the one path, so the golden shows them side by side.

`tally` carries the map form and `xs` the list form, because the exclusion was
written as a list of literal-shaped IR nodes and each member of it had the same
hole.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `P\{A: "", B: ""\}` -- an int field's zero is 0, and this one came from a walk with no case for the ident it was reading
deny out/go/fyne/model.go `P\{A: "", B: ""\}` -- fyne shares golang.LowerVarInit with bubbletea, so it shared the bug
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `P\{A: "", B: ""\}` -- and so does gtk4, the third platform on that shared path
deny out/kotlin/android/MainScreen.kt `P\(a = "", b = ""\)` -- android reaches the same hole through kotlin.IRLiteralToKt
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `\[\]int\{"", ""\}` -- the list form of the same fault, and the one that fails to compile
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `map\[string\]int\{"one": "", "two": ""\}` -- the map form

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}

struct P {
    a int
    b int
}

component main node {
    var (
        a = 1
        b = 2
        pair P = {a=a, b=b}
        xs list[int] = [a, b]
        tally map[string, int] = {one=a, two=b}
        constPair P = {a=1, b=2}
    )

    text(value=string(pair.a + pair.b))
    text(value=string(xs[0] + constPair.b))
    text(value=string(tally.get("one", 0)))
}

window {
    main
}
